_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00224,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.5,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Vylor Inc. operates as a seed and genetics company. It delivers a pipeline in the industry's elite germplasm and transformative sciences, such as biotechnology and gene editing. The company was founded in 1802 and is based in Johnston, Iowa.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Charles Victor Magro B.Sc. (Chem), MBA | CEO & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $5.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 21K people. Revenue per employee of $468K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $100K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 12\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). R&D investment of 10% of revenue (moderate) signals commitment to product development and talent.","financial_summary":["Vylor Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $46.8B market cap on $10.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are expanding by +2.8pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 48%.","The business throws off $2.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 21 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 6.66\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -9.7% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.7%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average SGA growth (13% YoY) warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Vylor (VYLR) Could Be 18% Undervalued After Its Dividend Move","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/food-beverage-tobacco/nyse-vylr/vylor/news/vylor-vylr-could-be-18-undervalued-after-its-dividend-move","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793729716.572,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.778,"tier":0,"scope":"com